<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.5.3: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00923</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.5.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bf6d86de-1971-4301-b044-de4850c17d7c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section>
    <para dir="ltr">Rental car company A charges $50 a day plus $0.50 a mile, \(m\), and is modeled by function \(A\).
  Rental car company B charges $20 a day plus $1.00 a mile, \(m\), and is modeled by function \(B\).
  Which statement is true for the cost of one day after \(m\) miles?
</para>
  </section>
</content>
</document>
